{"duration_api_ms":4564,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b1c282dd-e228-451e-baab-84548bfa139d","total_cost_usd":0.0006189,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":662,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":708,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":375},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":662,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":708,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":662,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":662},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-5-5":{"inputTokens":1205,"outputTokens":732,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":662,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0006189,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":375,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":662,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"safety_stops":0,"is_error":false,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Are APs paid by the sponsor?** Generally, no. APs are usually broker-dealers or market makers who earn money from arbitrage between the ETF and its underlying basket, plus trading spreads and commissions. Creation and redemption fees are charged to the APs and go to the fund to cover transaction costs, not to the AP. Some sponsors do pay for liquidity through incentive or liquidity-provider programs, but that is a separate arrangement, not payment for creating and redeeming.\n\n**Must APs keep creating and redeeming?** No. Creation and redemption are voluntary. APs sign participant agreements with the fund's distributor, and those agreements don't require ongoing activity. Market makers also have no general regulatory duty to quote or arbitrage. However, a fund needs at least some active APs to keep its price close to NAV. If APs stop, the ETF can trade at persistent premiums or discounts, and the sponsor may have to add APs, change the structure, or in extreme cases liquidate the fund.","ttft_ms":2459,"type":"result","duration_ms":3957,"uuid":"d78eff39-0de7-4c1a-9e1e-eb86857cab96","ttft_stream_ms":413,"time_to_request_ms":53,"first_content_frame_ms":414,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
